  cites Safari chapter GuardRail
  cites Safari chapter World
  cites Safari chapter RailPlan
  cites Judge chapter Grade

 RailPlan: the path a guard rail takes around a corner, sampled a metre at a
 time.

 THE SAMPLING RULE IS THE WHOLE OF WHAT IS GRADED HERE. A leg is walked in whole
 steps of about a metre, and `leg-steps` is where that "about" is decided:
 round the distance, then floor the result at ONE. Both halves matter and they
 fail differently -- without the rounding a 1.6-metre leg gets one step and bends
 visibly; without the floor a leg shorter than half a metre gets ZERO steps, and
 dividing by that is how a rail becomes a NaN rather than a short rail.

 THE POINTS RUN FROM THE FIRST STEP TO THE LAST, NOT FROM THE START. `push-leg`
 begins at index 1, so the point it was given is NOT re-emitted -- the previous
 leg already ended there. That is what lets the corner path be four pieces
 concatenated without a doubled vertex at each seam, and a doubled vertex would
 give GuardRail a zero-length post with no run direction. The count is the
 assertion: n steps produce exactly n points and the last one is the destination.

 We say:

Section: How Many Steps

 Round to the nearest whole metre, and never fewer than one.

  steps-got : List Integer
  steps-got =
    [ leg-steps 0.0, leg-steps 0.4, leg-steps 0.5, leg-steps 1.0,
      leg-steps 1.4, leg-steps 1.5, leg-steps 2.5, leg-steps 10.0,
      leg-steps 49.6, leg-steps 50.0 ]

  steps-want : List Integer
  steps-want = [1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 2, 3, 10, 50, 50]

Section: Walking A Leg

 Ten metres straight ahead in ten steps: ten points, one per metre, the last of
 them the destination and the start NOT among them.

  origin-pt : RiderPt
  origin-pt = RiderPt { right = 0.0, forward = 0.0 }

  straight : List RiderPt
  straight = push-leg origin-pt (RiderPt { right = 0.0, forward = 10.0 })

  straight-got : List Real
  straight-got =
    [ real-from-int (list-length straight),
      (list-at straight 0).forward, (list-at straight 4).forward, (list-at straight 9).forward,
      (list-at straight 0).right, (list-at straight 9).right ]

  straight-want : List Real
  straight-want = [10.0, 1.0, 5.0, 10.0, 0.0, 0.0]

 A three-four-five diagonal, so the fifty steps land on whole tenths and the last
 point is exactly the corner it was aimed at.

  diagonal : List RiderPt
  diagonal = push-leg origin-pt (RiderPt { right = 30.0, forward = 40.0 })

  diagonal-got : List Real
  diagonal-got =
    [ real-from-int (list-length diagonal),
      (list-at diagonal 49).right, (list-at diagonal 49).forward,
      (list-at diagonal 24).right, (list-at diagonal 24).forward ]

  diagonal-want : List Real
  diagonal-want = [50.0, 30.0, 40.0, 15.0, 20.0]

 A leg of no length still emits its destination, once. That is the floor doing
 its job: zero steps would divide by zero and put a NaN in the path.

  degenerate-got : List Real
  degenerate-got =
    let d = push-leg (RiderPt { right = 3.0, forward = 4.0 }) (RiderPt { right = 3.0, forward = 4.0 })
    in [ real-from-int (list-length d), (list-at d 0).right, (list-at d 0).forward ]

  degenerate-want : List Real
  degenerate-want = [1.0, 3.0, 4.0]

 Asked from index 0 rather than 1, the same walk carries the starting point too,
 so it is one longer. That is the difference `push-leg` exists to make.

  from-zero-got : List Real
  from-zero-got =
    let z = leg-points origin-pt 0.0 10.0 10 0
    in [ real-from-int (list-length z), (list-at z 0).forward, (list-at z 10).forward ]

  from-zero-want : List Real
  from-zero-want = [11.0, 0.0, 10.0]

Section: The Run Out

 The rail runs ten metres past each corner along the outer edge, one point per
 metre, counting from the corner itself -- so eleven points, not ten.

  segs : List Segment
  segs = [segment-at 0, segment-at 1, segment-at 2]

  chain : List Integer
  chain = [0, 1, 2]

  origin : Pose
  origin = Pose { along = 0.0, across = 0.0, yaw = 0.0, hw = 2.0 }

  runout-got : List Integer
  runout-got =
    [ rail-runout,
      list-length (rail-run-out segs chain origin (chain-map 0) 4.0 0),
      list-length (rail-run-up segs chain origin (chain-map 0) 500.0 4.0 rail-runout) ]

  runout-want : List Integer
  runout-want = [10, 11, 11]

 The run-up counts DOWN to the end edge, so its last point is the corner and the
 first leg starts from there rather than doubling it.

  runup-got : List Real
  runup-got =
    let u = rail-run-up segs chain origin (chain-map 0) 500.0 4.0 rail-runout
    in [ (list-at u 0).forward, (list-at u 10).forward ]

  runup-want : List Real
  runup-want = [490.0, 500.0]

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "rp-steps " steps-got steps-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "rp-straig" straight-got straight-want 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "rp-diag  " diagonal-got diagonal-want 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "rp-degen " degenerate-got degenerate-want 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "rp-zero  " from-zero-got from-zero-want 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "rp-runout" runout-got runout-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "rp-runup " runup-got runup-want 0.0001)
  end
